# Generated by every build and every test run, and TRACKED until 2026-08-09 —
# so each build dirtied the shared tree for whoever looked next, and each agent
# had to decide whether someone else's churn was theirs to commit. In a tree
# with several sessions in it that is not noise, it is a steady source of
# wrongly-attributed commits.
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
web/test-results/

# wasm-bindgen TYPE DECLARATIONS — IGNORED, while `twobee_cam_wasm.js` and
# `twobee_cam_wasm_bg.wasm` in the same directory are TRACKED. The asymmetry is
# the decision (2026-08-12), not an oversight, and here is the whole of it:
#
#   · `npm run wasm` — the ONE documented way to rebuild this directory — passes
#     `--no-typescript`. These two files are therefore NOT part of the artefact
#     set this project generates; they arrive only from a run that dropped the
#     flag, which is how they came to be sitting untracked beside two tracked
#     siblings. ✅ OBSERVED, not only read off the script: another lane rebuilt
#     the wasm at 12:08 on 2026-08-12, mid-decision — `twobee_cam_wasm_bg.wasm`
#     grew by 117kB, the `.js` was rewritten byte-identical, and NO `.d.ts`
#     appeared. A real rebuild is what settled this, not the flag's reputation.
#   · The `.js` and `.wasm` are tracked because they are the RUNTIME artefact:
#     `vite` loads them, and a contributor with no Rust toolchain must still be
#     able to run the app. Nothing loads a `.d.ts` at runtime.
#   · They are inert for every check we own. MEASURED 2026-08-12, both
#     directions: `npm run typecheck` and `npm run test:node` (1096) are green
#     with them and without them, and a PLANTED type error against the module
#     (`const n: number = clearance_for(1, 2)`) is caught IDENTICALLY either way
#     — the tracked `.js` carries the wasm-bindgen JSDoc and `allowJs` reads it.
#     So the declarations buy no type safety that is not already bought.
#   · 🔴 AND TRACKING THEM WOULD BUY A LIE. `--no-typescript` emits no `.d.ts`
#     AND DOES NOT DELETE A STALE ONE, so a tracked declaration would survive
#     every canonical rebuild of the `.js` and `.wasm` beside it, asserting a
#     contract the module no longer has — with both checks above staying green,
#     because they are green either way. An ignored file cannot drift; a tracked
#     generated file that the build never rewrites always does.
#
# ⚠ THE REASON HAS A TRIGGER: `tests/wasm-artefacts.test.ts` goes red if the
# `--no-typescript` flag leaves `package.json`, because that is the fact this
# whole block rests on and a dead reason reads exactly like a live one.
web/src/wasm/*.d.ts

# Cognito / env secrets — never commit. See web/.env.example for the template.
web/.env
web/.env.local
web/.env.*.local

# grblHAL firmware source + a 35 MB stm32f4 tarball, fetched here while chasing
# the controller's real capabilities. 🔴 IGNORED RATHER THAN COMMITTED FOR TWO
# REASONS: it is `pcb`'s lane per the boundary table in AGENTS.md, and it is
# untracked binary bulk sitting in a tree five sessions share — one widened
# `gcommit` pathspec and it lands in the shared history, where it cannot be
# taken back out cheaply. It is NOT evidence about this lane's output.
grblhal/
